# This CITATION.cff file was written for the bio-v1-replication repository.
# Validate it before release:  pip install cffconvert  then  cffconvert --validate
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the archived software
  (this file) and the accompanying preprint (preferred-citation below).
type: software
title: >-
  bio-v1-replication: Reproducibility and sensitivity of a spiking V1 model
  with triplet STDP and adaptive thresholds
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-27
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24602903
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SagarKarki-np/bio-v1-replication"
authors:
  - family-names: Karki
    given-names: Sagar
    affiliation: Independent researcher, Kathmandu, Nepal
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7556-5171"
abstract: >-
  Independent Python implementation of the biologically grounded spiking
  model of primary visual cortex of Ruslim et al. (2025), with triplet
  spike-timing-dependent plasticity and adaptive firing thresholds, built
  from the published article and the released MATLAB demonstration code.
  Includes experiment configurations for the demo-parameterized and
  paper-derived branches across five target firing rates, and analysis code
  for spike-triggered receptive fields, Gabor fitting, sparseness,
  correlations, excitation-inhibition balance and homeostatic calibration.
keywords:
  - primary visual cortex
  - spiking neural network
  - spike-timing-dependent plasticity
  - homeostasis
  - sparse coding
  - reproducibility
  - spike-triggered average

preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Reproducibility and sensitivity of a spiking V1 model with triplet STDP
    and adaptive thresholds
  authors:
    - family-names: Karki
      given-names: Sagar
